{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Change up for review: Gerrit 1490 — Verified +1, LLM-Review blocked on a stalled bot\n\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1490 (commit e46830652f, branch\n`e7a9-secret-screen`).\n\n**Verified +1** — the full CI matrix is green: lint + type-check, pip-audit, pytest on\nubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13 and macos py3.13, plus the eval-discipline, optionality,\nartifact-provenance, ticket-trailer, verify-identity and golden-path gates.\n(https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/31173336754)\n\n**LLM-Review is still pending**, and the cause is not this change. No open change in the\nqueue has an LLM-Review vote — 1488, 1490, 1491, 1494 and 1495 are all unvoted, and the\nmost recent vote anywhere is 1477 at 11:28. A `recheck-review` comment was posted on 1490\nand did not produce a review either, so the review bot looks stalled repo-wide rather than\nbacklogged behind this change specifically.\n\nThe ticket therefore stays `in_progress`: per the project rule a ticket is not closed until\nits change is `LLM-Review +1` AND `Verified +1` and has merged. Nothing about the change\nneeds to move for that; it needs the reviewer to run. Anyone picking this up can re-post\n`recheck-review` on 1490 once the bot is healthy, then Submit and close."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786102962597273001,"uuid":"be8ec990-9e63-42c7-af91-367ed348aa3c"}